==Scottish Premiership==
{{Main|2017–18 Scottish Premiership}}

The [[2017–18 Scottish Premiership|Scottish Premiership]] fixture list was announced on 23 June 2017.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/12814 | title=Invincibles kick off bid for seven-in-a-row with home game v Hearts | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=23 June 2017 | access-date=15 June 2018 | archive-date=15 June 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180615135029/http://www.celticfc.net/news/12814 | url-status=live }}</ref> Celtic began the defence of their title with a 4–1 victory against [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Heart of Midlothian]] at [[Celtic Park]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13042 | title=Manager's delight as champions lay down a marker on Flag Day | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=5 August 2017 | access-date=5 August 2017 | archive-date=5 August 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170805222734/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13042 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 4 November, Celtic broke their own British record for the number of games without defeat in all domestic competitions, a record set by [[Willie Maley]]'s team that stood for 100 years.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13496 | title=Brendan Rodgers: Breaking record is a really special feeling | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=4 November 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191501/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13496 | url-status=live }}</ref> However, the unbeaten run ended at 69 games, following a 4–0 defeat to Heart of Midlothian at [[Tynecastle Park]] on 17 December.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13707 | title=Manager: Celts will look forward and return to winning ways | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=17 December 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191517/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13707 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 29 April 2018, Celtic won their seventh consecutive title and 49th overall after a 5–0 win against [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14297 | title=Manager: I'm so proud of my players for winning title in style | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=29 April 2018 | access-date=29 April 2018 | archive-date=30 April 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180430045338/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14297 | url-status=live }}</ref>

