==Scottish League Cup==
{{Main|2017–18 Scottish League Cup}}
On 30 July, Celtic were drawn to face [[Kilmarnock F.C.|Kilmarnock]] at [[Celtic Park]] in the second round of the [[2017–18 Scottish League Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/12990 | title=Celtic to meet Kilmarnock in League Cup last 16 | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=30 July 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191534/http://www.celticfc.net/news/12990 | url-status=live }}</ref> Captained by [[Kieran Tierney]] for the first time, in the absence of the suspended [[Scott Brown (footballer, born June 1985)|Scott Brown]], Celtic won 5–0 to secure a berth in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13054 | title=Brendan Rodgers: Brilliant Bhoys were a joy to watch | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=8 August 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191529/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13054 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 9 August, Celtic were drawn to face [[Dundee F.C.|Dundee]] at [[Dens Park]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13060 | title=Celts face Dundee in League Cup quarter-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=9 August 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191523/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13060 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys continued their defence of the trophy, running out 4–0 winners with a double from [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]] and goals from [[Scott Sinclair]] and [[Callum McGregor]] securing a return to [[Hampden Park]] for the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13274 | title=Manager hails Boyata return as Celts cruise to Dens Park triumph | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=20 September 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191520/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13274 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 21 September, Celtic were drawn to face [[Hibernian F.C.|Hibernian]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13279 | title=Celtic face Hibernian in League Cup semi-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=21 September 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191450/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13279 | url-status=live }}</ref> A keenly fought contest ended in a 4–2 victory for Celtic with [[Mikael Lustig]] and [[Moussa Dembélé (French footballer)|Moussa Dembélé]] both netting twice to seal Celtic's place in the final. On 26 November, Celtic retained the [[Scottish League Cup]] by defeating [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]] [[2017–18 Scottish League Cup#Final|2–0]]. This was the 17th League Cup triumph in the club's history and the fourth trophy of [[Brendan Rodgers]]' reign.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13587 | title=Manager: Four trophies in a year is a phenomenal achievement | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=26 November 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191526/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13587 | url-status=live }}</ref>

