==Scottish Cup==
{{Main|2017–18 Scottish Cup}}
On 20 November, Celtic were drawn to face [[Brechin City F.C.|Brechin City]] at [[Celtic Park]] in the fourth round of the [[2017–18 Scottish Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13562 | title=Celtic to face Brechin City in fourth round of the Scottish Cup | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=20 November 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191505/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13562 | url-status=live }}</ref> Goals from [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]], [[Scott Sinclair]], [[Olivier Ntcham]], [[Dedryck Boyata]] and [[Odsonne Édouard]] secured a 5–0 victory for the cup holders.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13856 | title=Manager pleased with professional performance in Paradise | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=20 January 2018 | access-date=21 January 2018 | archive-date=22 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180122071942/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13856 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 21 January 2018, Celtic were drawn to face [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] in the fifth round.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13857 | title=Celtic face Partick Thistle at Paradise in Scottish Cup fifth round | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=21 January 2018 | access-date=21 January 2018 | archive-date=22 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180122072014/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13857 | url-status=live }}</ref> A [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]] hat-trick sealed a 3–2 win and Celtic's place in the quarter-finals for the fourth consecutive season.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13954 | title=Manager hails fantastic Forrest after Glasgow derby triumph | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=10 February 2018 | access-date=11 February 2018 | archive-date=12 February 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180212083157/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13954 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 11 February, Celtic were drawn to face [[Greenock Morton F.C.|Greenock Morton]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13955 | title=Celtic face Greenock Morton in Scottish Cup quarter-final tie | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=11 February 2018 | access-date=11 February 2018 | archive-date=12 February 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180212083233/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13955 | url-status=live }}</ref> Goals from [[Moussa Dembélé (French footballer)|Moussa Dembélé]] and [[Odsonne Édouard]] secured a place in the semi-finals and a return to [[Hampden Park|Hampden]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14053 | title=Manager: Edouard was the spark Celts needed in win over Morton | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=3 March 2018 | access-date=4 March 2018 | archive-date=4 March 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180304231636/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14053 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 4 March, Celtic were drawn to face [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14055 | title=Celtic face Rangers in the Scottish Cup semi-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=4 March 2018 | access-date=5 March 2018 | archive-date=6 March 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180306082743/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14055 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys sealed their place in the final with [[Tom Rogic]], [[Callum McGregor]], [[Moussa Dembélé (French footballer)|Moussa Dembélé]] and [[Olivier Ntcham]] all on the scoresheet.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14225 | title=Manager: We showed an edge in superb semi-final win | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=15 April 2018 | access-date=23 April 2018 | archive-date=24 April 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180424071636/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14225 | url-status=live }}</ref> Celtic beat [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]] 2–0 in the [[2018 Scottish Cup Final|final]] on 19 May 2018, with goals from [[Callum McGregor]] and [[Olivier Ntcham]] ensuring Celtic's defence of the trophy.

