==Europe==

===UEFA Champions League===
{{Main|2017–18 UEFA Champions League}}

====Second qualifying round====
[[File:Celtic-banners-linfield.png|thumb|right|200px|Banner display against [[Linfield F.C.|Linfield]]]]

On 19 June, Celtic were drawn to face [[Linfield F.C.|Linfield]] (Northern Ireland) or [[S.P. La Fiorita|La Fiorita]] ([[San Marino]]) in the Second Qualifying Round of the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/12798 | title=Celtic to play Linfield or La Fiorita in Champions League | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=19 June 2017 | access-date=1 July 2017 | archive-date=22 June 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622032936/http://www.celticfc.net/news/12798 | url-status=live }}</ref> On 4 July, it was determined that Linfield would be Celtic's opponents, having defeated La Fiorita 1–0 on aggregate. The first leg took place at [[Windsor Park]] on 14 July, two days after [[The Twelfth]]. Celtic refused its ticket allocation due to concerns for supporter safety.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/12822 | title=UEFA Champions League qualifying tie information | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=23 June 2017 | access-date=1 July 2017 | archive-date=26 June 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170626035830/http://www.celticfc.net/news/12822 | url-status=live }}</ref> Linfield later reiterated this, announcing that Celtic supporters would not be allowed to purchase tickets for the match.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.newsletter.co.uk/news/linfield-say-celtic-fans-will-be-refused-admittance-to-champions-league-game-in-belfast-1-8042297|title=Linfield say Celtic fans will be refused admittance to Champions League game in Belfast|website=www.newsletter.co.uk|language=en|access-date=2017-07-08|archive-date=2017-07-08|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170708094606/http://www.newsletter.co.uk/news/linfield-say-celtic-fans-will-be-refused-admittance-to-champions-league-game-in-belfast-1-8042297|url-status=live}}</ref> However, on the day of the match, the Northern Irish champions announced that away fans who had purchased tickets for the home end would be given their own section in the stadium.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.linfieldfc.com/latestnews.aspx?id=17799 | title=Important Club Statement re: Access Arrangements for tonight's game | publisher=[[Linfield F.C.|Linfield]] | date=14 July 2017 | access-date=14 July 2017 | archive-date=19 July 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170719204034/http://www.linfieldfc.com/latestnews.aspx?id=17799 | url-status=live }}</ref> Celtic recorded a 2–0 victory in the first leg. The match did not pass without incident, as several objects were thrown towards Celtic players during the second half. [[Leigh Griffiths]] was controversially booked for simply drawing this to the referee's attention.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/40615248|title=Celtic: Linfield look into Leigh Griffiths Champions League bottle incident|date=2017-07-14|work=BBC Sport|access-date=17 July 2017|language=en-GB|archive-date=2017-07-17|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170717183034/http://www.bbc.com/sport/football/40615248|url-status=live}}</ref> Griffiths was later suspended by [[UEFA]] for one match, for tying a scarf to the goalpost after the game, which was deemed to have provoked a section of the home crowd.<ref name="linleigh">{{cite news|title=Leigh Griffiths: Celtic striker banned by Uefa for 'provoking spectators'|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/40671971|access-date=20 January 2018|work=BBC Sport|date=20 July 2017|archive-date=20 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170820193630/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/40671971|url-status=live}}</ref> Celtic won 4–0 in the second leg, securing a place in the next round and a tie against [[Rosenborg BK|Rosenborg]].<ref name="linleigh" /> The club was again charged by UEFA for several offences, including illicit banners being displayed by the [[Green Brigade]] section of the home support.<ref>{{cite news|title=Celtic face Uefa charge over 'illicit banner' against Linfield|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/40674198|access-date=20 January 2018|work=BBC Sport|date=20 July 2017|archive-date=13 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170813044837/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/40674198|url-status=live}}</ref> Celtic subsequently condemned the banners and suspended the group for the next two matches at [[Celtic Park]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Celtic announce Green Brigade ban to be lifted after Hearts match - but some fans will still be denied entry|url=https://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/celtic-announce-green-brigade-ban-10907700|access-date=20 January 2018|work=Daily Record|date=31 July 2017|archive-date=21 January 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180121000015/https://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/celtic-announce-green-brigade-ban-10907700|url-status=live}}</ref>

