====Play-off round====
On 4 August, Celtic were drawn to face [[FC Astana|Astana]] ([[Kazakhstan]]) in the Play-Off Round of the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13022 | title=Celtic face FC Astana in UEFA Champions League play-off | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=4 August 2017 | access-date=25 August 2017 | archive-date=25 August 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170825192322/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13022 | url-status=live }}</ref> The sides met one round earlier in the [[2016–17 UEFA Champions League#Third qualifying round|previous season's competition]], with the Scottish champions recording a 3–2 victory on aggregate. Celtic cruised to a 5–0 victory in the first leg, with two own goals bookending a double from [[Scott Sinclair]] and a goal from [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]]. [[Nir Bitton]] deputised at centre half – injuries ruled [[Dedryck Boyata]] and [[Erik Sviatchenko]] out of the tie – and was singled out for praise by [[Brendan Rodgers]] in the aftermath.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://stv.tv/sport/football/1395827-rodgers-celtic-win-showed-how-much-players-have-developed | title=Rodgers: Celtic win showed how much players have developed | publisher=stv.tv | date=16 August 2017 | access-date=18 August 2017 | archive-date=19 August 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170819102451/https://stv.tv/sport/football/1395827-rodgers-celtic-win-showed-how-much-players-have-developed/ | url-status=live }}</ref> The second leg saw Celtic record their first loss in all competitions since November 2016, when they were defeated by [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] at [[Celtic Park]]. Although the Hoops lost 4–3 on the night, goals from [[Scott Sinclair]], [[Olivier Ntcham]] and [[Leigh Griffiths]] ensured Celtic's place amongst Europe's elite for the second consecutive season. In addition, Celtic's 8–4 aggregate win became the highest-scoring tie in [[UEFA Champions League]] play-off history.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://twitter.com/ChampionsLeague/status/900046104879878144 | title=Celtic v Astana | date=22 August 2017 | access-date=25 August 2017 | archive-date=5 September 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170905015114/https://twitter.com/ChampionsLeague/status/900046104879878144 | url-status=live }}</ref>

