====Group stage====
On 24 August, the draw for the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League#Group stage|2017–18 UEFA Champions League group stage]] was made. Celtic were drawn in [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League#Group B|Group B]] along with [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] (Pot 1), [[Paris Saint-Germain F.C.|Paris Saint-Germain]] (Pot 2) and [[R.S.C. Anderlecht|Anderlecht]] (Pot 3).<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13138 | title=Bayern Munich, PSG and Anderlecht are heading to Paradise | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=24 August 2017 | access-date=25 August 2017 | archive-date=25 August 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170825191825/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13138 | url-status=live }}</ref> Celtic last met the [[2016–17 Bundesliga|German]] and [[2016–17 Belgian First Division A|Belgian]] champions in the [[2003–04 UEFA Champions League#Group A|2003–04 season]], and have not faced the [[Ligue 1]] side since [[1995–96 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup#Second round|1995]]. Paris Saint-Germain inflicted Celtic's heaviest ever home defeat in European competition on Matchday 1, with goals from the most expensive forward line in history: [[Neymar]], [[Kylian Mbappé]] and [[Edinson Cavani]]. Following the match, [[Brendan Rodgers]] suggested his team played like under-12s in the early stages of the game.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/41249313 | title=Celtic 0-5 PSG: Brendan Rodgers says team played like under-12s in first half | publisher=[[BBC Sport]] | date=12 September 2017 | access-date=7 October 2017 | archive-date=21 October 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171021215815/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/41249313 | url-status=live }}</ref> Celtic did however respond on Matchday 2 in [[Brussels]], recording a priceless victory over Anderlecht. [[Leigh Griffiths]], [[Patrick Roberts]] and [[Scott Sinclair]] were on the scoresheet as the club secured its second away victory in Champions League history, and its first away victory since [[2012–13 UEFA Champions League group stage#Spartak Moscow v Celtic|2012]], when Celtic defeated [[FC Spartak Moscow|Spartak Moscow]]. Despite a valiant display against Bayern Munich at [[Celtic Park]] and scoring the first goal against Paris Saint-Germain in European competition that season, Celtic lost all four remaining games in the group, but did parachute into the [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League#Round of 32|2017–18 UEFA Europa League knockout phase]] after finishing with a better head-to-head record against Anderlecht.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13643 | title=Manager: We'll be better when Europa League comes around | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=5 December 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=2 January 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180102191531/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13643 | url-status=live }}</ref>

