===UEFA Europa League===
{{Main|2017–18 UEFA Europa League}}
On 11 December, Celtic were drawn to face [[FC Zenit Saint Petersburg|Zenit Saint Petersburg]] in the Last 32 of the [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13664 | title=Celtic face Zenit St Petersburg in UEFA Europa League last 32 | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=11 December 2017 | access-date=2 January 2018 | archive-date=25 December 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171225091941/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13664 | url-status=live }}</ref> [[Callum McGregor]]'s strike gave Celtic a narrow first-leg advantage,<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/13980 | title=Manager: Players produced an outstanding European performance | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=15 February 2018 | access-date=2 July 2018 | archive-date=2 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180702204903/http://www.celticfc.net/news/13980 | url-status=live }}</ref> however, a 3–0 defeat in [[Saint Petersburg]] brought the Bhoys' involvement in European competition to an end for the 2017–18 season.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14012 | title=Manager: Bhoys lacked bravery on the ball in Zenit loss | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=22 February 2018 | access-date=2 July 2018 | archive-date=1 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180701215254/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14012 | url-status=live }}</ref>

